WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.563
Tony Stark: We're the Avengers.

00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:03.883
We gotta finish this.

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:06.350
Narrator: Marvel just dropped

00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:09.370
another teaser for "Avengers: Endgame,"

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:11.120
and while it doesn't show much,

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:14.630
it does reveal a few new
tidbits about the movie.

00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:16.893
Warning: possible spoilers ahead.

00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:22.370
Bruce Banner: If we do this,
we'd be going in shorthanded.

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:23.760
Narrator: The trailer starts out

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:25.870
with the team deciding to go after Thanos

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:27.280
to avenge their friends.

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:29.550
We see the Benatar approaching New York,

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:31.860
then Rocket and Nebula
sitting on its steps.

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:34.430
Both have suffered devastating losses

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:36.300
with Nebula losing her sister

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.680
and Rocket losing his entire team,

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:40.735
including his pal Groot.

00:00:40.735 --> 00:00:42.163
Rocket: No, no, no, no!

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:44.753
Groot,

00:00:44.753 --> 00:00:46.030
no.

00:00:46.030 --> 00:00:48.470
Narrator: It looks like Rocket
is wearing his normal outfit,

00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:51.440
which is important for what
comes later in the trailer.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:55.230
Tony and Pepper hug. We don't
know how long he's been gone

00:00:55.230 --> 00:00:57.410
or how long it took for him to get back,

00:00:57.410 --> 00:01:00.300
but this is a reunion fans
have been waiting for.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:02.020
Is this them saying goodbye again

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:04.080
as he goes to take on Thanos?

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:06.110
Hawkeye has a lot more tattoos

00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:07.960
than the last time we saw him.

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:10.470
It looks like someone is
not taking the snap well.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:12.613
Has he lost his entire family?

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:14.810
In the group shot,

00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:17.700
Rocket is the only one
suited up for action.

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:19.100
Is this when the team decides

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:21.470
to finally take the battle to Thanos?

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:24.810
This one's for all the fans
shipping Tony and Steve.

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:25.643
Tony: You trust me?

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:27.773
Steve Rogers: I do.

00:01:27.773 --> 00:01:28.606
Narrator: Next, we see

00:01:28.606 --> 00:01:31.380
most of the remaining
Avengers on the Benatar.

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:34.110
Rocket is not wearing the
jumpsuit he had on earlier,

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:35.930
and the team is not wearing the spacesuits

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:37.690
we saw in an earlier trailer.

00:01:37.690 --> 00:01:40.360
There's also no Hawkeye, Nebula,

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:43.030
Ant-Man, or Tony in this shot.

00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:44.940
Are they somewhere else on the ship

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:47.170
or taking care of a different mission?

00:01:47.170 --> 00:01:49.440
Black Widow has the same short, blond hair

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:51.190
she had in "Infinity War."

00:01:51.190 --> 00:01:52.770
With this trailer and others

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:54.970
showing longer, more red hair,

00:01:54.970 --> 00:01:57.870
does this take place
soon after "Infinity War"

00:01:57.870 --> 00:02:00.500
with other parts of the
movie happening much later?

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:01.690
It has been pointed out

00:02:01.690 --> 00:02:04.850
that Tony's hair looks a
lot grayer in some shots.

00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:08.300
Could the team be going to both
space and the Quantum Realm?

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:10.040
The movie is three hours long,

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:12.150
so there's definitely time for both.

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:14.760
We get a voiceover of Thanos saying:

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:17.330
Thanos: You could not live
with your own failure.

00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:19.320
Narrator: Then a shot of Thanos' ship.

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:20.750
It looks like Nebula and Rhodey

00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:24.370
are both looking at Thanos'
giant Sanctuary II ship,

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:26.860
so it seems Nebula was
elsewhere on the Benatar

00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:28.310
in that group shot.

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:29.970
Thanos beams down the way he did

00:02:29.970 --> 00:02:31.930
before he had the Space Stone.

00:02:31.930 --> 00:02:33.838
In "Infinity War," he used the Space Stone

00:02:33.838 --> 00:02:36.438
to teleport around, but
it looks like he's back

00:02:36.438 --> 00:02:38.460
to using his ship's beam transport.

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:41.070
Does this mean he no
longer has the Space Stone?

00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:42.640
Or is it not working?

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:45.610
Finally, we see Tony, Cap, and Thor

00:02:45.610 --> 00:02:48.000
approaching Thanos on
what looks like Titan,

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:51.200
where Tony and the others
fought him in "Infinity War."

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:53.440
Will this be some sort of time warp?

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:56.713
Was Thanos unable to restore
Titan to its former glory?

00:02:57.910 --> 00:03:00.340
What do you think, did we miss anything?

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:01.803
Let us know in the comments.

